msgstr ""

msgid "Enabled"
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatically manage the stack from OMV. On Apply the stack is (re)created; disabling the service removes the containers on Apply (data and database are kept)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Version"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nextcloud image tag"
msgstr ""

msgid "Docker image tag for the nextcloud image (e.g. 34.0.4-apache). Prefer pinning a specific version; upgrade with the Upgrade button or change the tag here and Apply."
msgstr ""

msgid "Storage"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stack file (Compose plugin)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stack file location. The stack files are rendered by the Compose plugin into its shared folder and are managed there, so this path cannot be changed here. Set the folder in Services -> Compose -> Settings."
msgstr ""

msgid "Data shared folder"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared folder mapped to the Nextcloud data directory inside the container (/var/www/html). To move the data or the database folder, select the new folder in the form but do NOT save yet - click 'Test directories' to validate the changed folders and 'Migrate data' to copy them. Save only after the migration succeeded; the data in the old folders is removed when the settings are saved."
msgstr ""

msgid "Test directories"
msgstr ""

msgid "Migrate data"
msgstr ""

msgid "Validate the selected shared folders"
msgstr ""

msgid "Directory migration"
msgstr ""

msgid "Do you really want to migrate the data of the changed folders? The service is stopped, the data is copied with rsync (the originals stay untouched) and the completed migration is recorded. Nothing is saved until you click Save; the stack runs on the new locations after Apply and the data in the old folders is removed when the settings are saved."
msgstr ""

msgid "Removing the previous data"
msgstr ""

msgid "Database shared folder"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared folder mapped to the MariaDB data directory inside the container (/var/lib/mysql). To move the data or the database folder, select the new folder in the form but do NOT save yet - click 'Test directories' to validate the changed folders and 'Migrate data' to copy them. Save only after the migration succeeded; the data in the old folders is removed when the settings are saved."
msgstr ""

